      "hints": [
        "General term in $\\left(\\frac{2}{x} - 3x\\right)^5$ is $\\binom{5}{r}\\left(\\frac{2}{x}\\right)^{5-r}(-3x)^r = \\binom{5}{r}2^{5-r}(-3)^r x^{2r-5}$.",
        "Set $2r - 5 = 1 \\implies r = 3$ to find the coefficient."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Write down the general term in the binomial expansion of $\\left(\\frac{2}{x} - 3x\\right)^5$:\n$$T_{r+1} = \\binom{5}{r}\\left(\\frac{2}{x}\\right)^{5-r}(-3x)^r = \\binom{5}{r}2^{5-r}(-3)^r x^{2r-5}$$",
        "Set the power of $x$ equal to $1$ to isolate the term in $x$:\n$$2r - 5 = 1 \\implies 2r = 6 \\implies r = 3$$",
        "Calculate the coefficient:\n$$\\text{Coefficient of } x = \\binom{5}{3}2^{5-3}(-3)^3 = 10(2^2)(-27) = 10(4)(-27) = -1080$$"
      ],
